{"id":"4d593b8d1d529b9a","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-jump-measure.md","title":"Jump Measure","display":"df-jump-measure — Jump Measure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-jump-measure","aliases":["58-df-jump-measure","Jump Measure"],"display":"df-jump-measure — Jump Measure","depends_on":["[[58-df-semimartingale]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-jump-measure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-jump-measure</span><span>Jump Measure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-jump-measure — Jump Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f0355544d1bb59cc\" href=\"?note=f0355544d1bb59cc\" title=\"58-df-semimartingale\">58-df-semimartingale</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)\">\\(\\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)\\)</span> (real-valued semimartingale predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f0355544d1bb59cc\" href=\"?note=f0355544d1bb59cc\" title=\"58-df-semimartingale\">58-df-semimartingale</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\">\\(\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\)</span> (sample point)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (candidate pathwise counting measure)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"W\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\">\\(W\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\)</span> (measurable set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{JumpMeasure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{JumpMeasure}_S\\)</span> (pathwise jump-measure predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}jump\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{JumpMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T,\\omega_0)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)\\land\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\land\\mu:\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\to\\overline{\\mathbb N}\\land\\forall W\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\;\\mu(W)=\\#\\{s\\in T\\setminus\\{0\\}:\\exists z\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(z=X_s(\\omega_0)-\\lim_{u\\uparrow s}X_u(\\omega_0)\\land(s,z)\\in W)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}jump\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{JumpMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T,\\omega_0)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)\\land\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\land\\mu:\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\to\\overline{\\mathbb N}\\land\\forall W\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\;\\mu(W)=\\#\\{s\\in T\\setminus\\{0\\}:\\exists z\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(z=X_s(\\omega_0)-\\lim_{u\\uparrow s}X_u(\\omega_0)\\land(s,z)\\in W)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The nonzero-jump guard is essential: counting all times with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Delta X_s=0\">\\(\\Delta X_s=0\\)</span> would not define the atomic jump measure.</li>\n<li>Compensator <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_t\">\\(\\nu_t\\)</span>: dual predictable projection; removes drift from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu^X\">\\(\\mu^X\\)</span></li>\n<li>Lévy-Khintchine: characteristic exponent <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\psi(u) = a|u|^2 + \\int(e^{i\\langle u,z\\rangle}-1)\\nu(dz)\">\\(\\psi(u) = a|u|^2 + \\int(e^{i\\langle u,z\\rangle}-1)\\nu(dz)\\)</span></li>\n<li>Pure jump: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a=0\">\\(a=0\\)</span> in LK formula; purely discontinuous processes</li>\n<li>Compensators and compensated jump measures are downstream atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Jacod and Shiryaev, Limit Theorems for Stochastic Processes</li>\n<li>Applebaum, Lévy Processes and Stochastic Calculus</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-semimartingale","status":"resolved","id":"f0355544d1bb59cc","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-semimartingale]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-semimartingale","status":"resolved","id":"f0355544d1bb59cc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)$ (real-valued semimartingale predicate, see [[58-df-semimartingale]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega_0\\in\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"W\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{JumpMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}jump\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{JumpMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T,\\omega_0)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Semimartingale}_S(X,\\mathbb F,\\Omega,\\mathcal A,\\mathbb P,T)\\land\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\land\\mu:\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\to\\overline{\\mathbb N}\\land\\forall W\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_+\\times(\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}))\\;\\mu(W)=\\#\\{s\\in T\\setminus\\{0\\}:\\exists z\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(z=X_s(\\omega_0)-\\lim_{u\\uparrow s}X_u(\\omega_0)\\land(s,z)\\in W)\\}","display":true},{"tex":"\\Delta X_s=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\nu_t","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu^X","display":false},{"tex":"\\psi(u) = a|u|^2 + \\int(e^{i\\langle u,z\\rangle}-1)\\nu(dz)","display":false},{"tex":"a=0","display":false}],"bytes":1785,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-725","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-jump-measure.md|58-df-jump-measure]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["f0355544d1bb59cc"]}